  "text_pages": [
    "Required English Proficiency for the Student Exchange Program | Tohoku University\nRequired English Proficiency for the Student Exchange Program\nTOP\n>\nFor International Students\n>\nExchange Programs\n>\nRequired English Proficiency for the Student Exchange Program\nApplicants seeking admission to English-Based exchange program (JYPE/COLABS/IPLA) whose native language is not English are required to prove English proficiency through one of the following ways.\nQualification\nMinimum Requirement\nIELTS (International English Language Testing System)\nOverall Band - 6.0\n(The online version of IELTS is also acceptable.)\nTOEFL®Test\n- Option 1: TOEFL iBT®\n- Option 2: TOEFL PBT®\nScore - 79 (option1)\nScore - 550 (option2)\nTOEIC (Test of English for International Communication)\nScore - 730\nCEFR (Common European Framework of Reference for Languages)*2\nB2 or equivalent\nIB (International Baccalaureate)\nEnglish A1 or A2 (Higher or Standard Level)\nGrade 4\nEnglish A: Language and Literature (Higher or Standard Level)\nGrade 4\nEnglish A: Literature (Higher or Standard Level)\nGrade 4\nEnglish Literature and Performance (Standard Level)\nGrade 4\nEnglish B (Higher Level)\nGrade 4\nEnglish B (Standard Level)\nGrade 5\nCertificate in Advanced English (CAE)\nGrade C\nCambridge English: First (FCE)\nB2\nFrench Baccalauréat (OIB-British, American Options) English subject\nScore: 12\nDAAD Scholarships\nQualified Applicant (B2 or equivalent)\nCET(China) - 4\nScore - 530\nCET(China) - 6\nScore - 500\n*1 A required certificate has to be within its validity period\n*2 EF-SET(https://www.efset.org/) Certificate is unacceptable\n*3 TOEFL is a registered trademark of ETS. This (publication/ product/ website) is not endorsed or approved by ETS.\n*4 Duolingo English Test certificate is not available.\n*5 TOEFL®-ITP is not available.\nEnglish requirement will be waived if a student satisfy one of the following conditions:\n- students who are currently enrolled in the universities in one of the following countries\n- students completed high school or university degree earned from one of the following countries.\nAustralia\nCanada\nNew Zealand\nSouth Africa\nSingapore\nUnited Kingdom\nUnited States\nIf applicants enroll in a course generally instructed in English, a\nCERTIFICATE\nissued by their home university which verifies their enrollment will be validated as a language certificate."
  ],
